91	Visit to Mevlana Museum and Karatay Madrasa, Konya	<p>Dive into the spiritual heart of Turkey with a visit to&nbsp; Mevlana Museum and&nbsp; Karatay Madrasa in Konya. Explore the mausoleum of Rumi, the legendary Sufi mystic, and witness artifacts, manuscripts, and dervish robes that illustrate the Mevlevi Order&rsquo;s mystical traditions. Then head to Karatay Madrasa to see beautiful Seljuk architecture and archaeological treasures from Kubadabad Palace. Guided explanations reveal the philosophical, artistic, and cultural significance of these historic sites. Ideal for spiritual seekers, history enthusiasts, and travelers interested in Turkish art and architecture, this excursion illuminates Konya&rsquo;s unique blend of faith, creativity, and history. Walk among intricately tiled courtyards, study ancient manuscripts, and experience the atmosphere that inspired centuries of poetry and spiritual practice. Make this&nbsp; Konya visit an unforgettable highlight of your&nbsp; Turkish holiday, combining culture, history, and spiritual insight.</p>	Visit Konya’s Mevlana Museum and Karatay Madrasa to explore Rumi’s legacy, Sufi art, and Seljuk architecture in Turkey.	visit-to-mevlana-museum-and-karatay-madrasa-konya	\N	t	2026-04-06 11:42:54.092465+00	2026-04-06 11:42:54.092465+00	f
92	Aphrodisias and Its Ancient Ruins Tour, Pamukkale	<p>Explore the expansive ruins of&nbsp; Aphrodisias , one of Turkey&rsquo;s best-preserved ancient cities, renowned for its marble sculptures and monumental architecture. Wander through the ancient streets, temples, stadium, and the beautifully designed Sebasteion, learning about the city&rsquo;s role in art, culture, and politics in antiquity. Many areas remain partially excavated, giving a sense of discovery as ruins emerge amid greenery. Guided tours reveal stories of gods, emperors, and local artisans who shaped the city&rsquo;s identity. Ideal for archaeologists, history enthusiasts, and curious travelers, Aphrodisias offers a unique glimpse into life in a Greek and Roman provincial city. Capture stunning photographs of marble reliefs, sculptures, and architectural details, connecting the past with the present. Include Aphrodisias in your Turkey travel itinerary for a cultural journey filled with mystery, history, and awe-inspiring ruins.</p>	Visit Aphrodisias in Pamukkale, a vast ancient city with temples, stadiums, and marble sculptures for history and culture lovers.\n	aphrodisias-and-its-ancient-ruins-tour-pamukkale	\N	t	2026-04-06 11:43:49.264858+00	2026-04-06 11:43:49.264858+00	f
93	Visit to Hierapolis and Pamukkale Travertines, Pamukkale	<p>Discover the stunning&nbsp; Pamukkale Travertines&nbsp; and ancient city of&nbsp; Hierapolis, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Marvel at the cascading white terraces formed by mineral-rich thermal waters over millennia. Walk barefoot on these natural formations while enjoying panoramic views of the valley. Explore the ruins of Hierapolis, including its Roman theater, necropolis, and ancient baths, revealing Turkey&rsquo;s rich historical tapestry. Guided tours provide insights into the city&rsquo;s significance as a spa destination in antiquity and its religious importance during the Roman and Byzantine periods. Ideal for photographers, history enthusiasts, and nature lovers, this excursion combines natural wonders with archaeological exploration. Relax in thermal waters, wander ancient streets, and absorb the serenity of this unique landscape. A visit to Pamukkale and Hierapolis is a must on any Turkish holiday, offering a perfect balance of beauty, culture, and history.</p>	Explore Pamukkale’s white terraces and ancient Hierapolis ruins, combining natural beauty, thermal springs, and history in Turkey.\n	visit-to-hierapolis-and-pamukkale-travertines-pamukkale	\N	t	2026-04-06 11:45:23.986724+00	2026-04-06 11:45:23.986724+00	f
94	 Blue Mosque Guided Tour, Istanbul	<p>Discover the beauty of Istanbul&rsquo;s&nbsp; Blue Mosque , officially known as Sultan Ahmed Mosque, a masterpiece of Ottoman architecture. Renowned for its six slender minarets and majestic dome, this mosque dominates the historic Sultanahmet skyline. Step inside to admire the striking blue Iznik tiles, delicate calligraphy, and serene prayer halls. A guided tour provides historical context, detailing the mosque&rsquo;s construction, religious significance, and cultural impact. Photography enthusiasts will delight in capturing its intricate interior and iconic exterior. The Blue Mosque is a symbol of Istanbul&rsquo;s unique blend of history, art, and spirituality, perfect for travelers seeking a meaningful cultural experience. This guided visit also offers insights into daily Islamic practices, enhancing your understanding of Turkish heritage. Make your Istanbul itinerary&nbsp; unforgettable by experiencing the grandeur, history, and elegance of the Blue Mosque, one of Turkey&rsquo;s most visited landmarks.</p>	Tour Istanbul’s Blue Mosque with its iconic minarets, blue Iznik tiles, and Ottoman architecture for an unforgettable Turkish holiday experience.	blue-mosque-guided-tour-istanbul	\N	t	2026-04-06 11:46:40.987843+00	2026-04-06 11:46:40.987843+00	t
95	Trip to the Göreme Open Air Museum, Cappadocia	<p>Visit the&nbsp; G&ouml;reme Open Air Museum , Cappadocia&rsquo;s most iconic cultural site, featuring a remarkable collection of rock-cut churches, monasteries, and chapels. Dating back to the 10th century, this UNESCO World Heritage Site showcases vibrant frescoes, Byzantine architecture, and well-preserved cave dwellings. Wander through ancient monastic complexes and learn about the lives of monks who once inhabited these surreal landscapes. Each church tells a story through detailed murals depicting biblical scenes, offering insight into Cappadocia&rsquo;s spiritual and artistic history. Ideal for history enthusiasts, photographers, and travelers seeking a blend of culture and natural beauty, this excursion highlights Cappadocia&rsquo;s unique geological formations alongside its rich heritage. Experience the fairy-tale landscapes of volcanic rock, soft valleys, and hidden cave sanctuaries. Make the G&ouml;reme Open Air Museum a must-see stop on your&nbsp; Turkey travel itinerary , providing both education and inspiration for an unforgettable holiday adventure.</p>	Explore Göreme Open Air Museum in Cappadocia with cave churches, Byzantine frescoes, and surreal landscapes on an unforgettable Turkish holiday.	trip-to-the-goreme-open-air-museum-cappadocia	\N	t	2026-04-06 11:47:38.665472+00	2026-04-06 11:47:38.665472+00	f
96	Full-Day Visit to Gallipoli Battlefields and Troy, Çanakkale	<p>Step back in time with a&nbsp; full-day tour of Gallipoli Battlefields and Troy , two historic highlights of Turkey. At Gallipoli, visit beach cemeteries, memorials, and monuments dedicated to fallen Allied soldiers from World War I, reflecting the courage and sacrifice of those who fought. Continue to the legendary city of Troy, famous for the Trojan War and its monumental wooden horse. Explore ancient ruins, including the city walls, temples, and the archaeological site, guided by expert historians who bring stories and myths to life. This tour combines military history, ancient mythology, and cultural exploration, perfect for history buffs, school groups, and travelers seeking meaningful experiences. Walking these iconic sites offers a deep connection to Turkey&rsquo;s past, with plenty of photo opportunities and reflective moments. Make your&nbsp; Turkish holiday* unforgettable with this immersive journey through history and legend, experiencing the enduring legacy of Gallipoli and Troy.</p>	Explore Gallipoli’s WWI battlefields and the legendary city of Troy on a full-day historical tour for a rich Turkish holiday experience.	full-day-visit-to-gallipoli-battlefields-and-troy-canakkale	\N	t	2026-04-06 11:48:34.542136+00	2026-04-06 11:48:34.542136+00	f
98	Tour of the Basilica Cistern, Istanbul	<p>Descend beneath Istanbul&rsquo;s streets into the mysterious&nbsp; Basilica Cistern , a hidden underground world of history and architecture. Built in the 6th century during Emperor Justinian&rsquo;s reign, this vast subterranean chamber features hundreds of columns rising from water, with majestic brick arches overhead. On a private guided tour, you&rsquo;ll learn about the cistern&rsquo;s engineering, its role in supplying water to the Byzantine Palace, and the legends surrounding Medusa&rsquo;s head carved into two columns. The atmosphere, enhanced by dim lighting and gentle water reflections, transports visitors back in time. Ideal for photography enthusiasts, history buffs, and travelers seeking off-the-beaten-path experiences, the Basilica Cistern is both awe-inspiring and educational. Witness the ingenuity of ancient architects and discover the secrets hidden beneath Istanbul&rsquo;s bustling streets. Make this iconic&nbsp; Turkish holiday destination&nbsp; a highlight of your Istanbul itinerary for an unforgettable underground adventure.</p>	Explore Istanbul’s Basilica Cistern with hundreds of columns, arches, and Medusa carvings on a private guided underground tour.	tour-of-the-basilica-cistern-istanbul	\N	t	2026-04-06 11:51:07.863244+00	2026-04-06 11:51:07.863244+00	t
100	Pamukkale & Hierapolis Tour	<p>Explore one of Turkey&rsquo;s most unique wonders with a guided visit to Pamukkale and the ancient city of Hierapolis. Famous for its dazzling white travertine terraces formed by mineral-rich thermal waters, Pamukkale offers a surreal landscape perfect for photography and relaxation. Walk barefoot across the terraces or enjoy the healing properties of its warm pools. Above, discover the ruins of Hierapolis, including ancient theatres, temples, and Roman baths that tell the story of this historic spa city. This full-day excursion blends nature, history, and wellness, making it one of the top experiences in Turkey. Add this unforgettable tour to your Turkey holiday package with Allbound Vacations.</p>	Pamukkale tour: white terraces, thermal pools & ancient Hierapolis ruins. A unique natural wonder in Turkey.	pamukkale-hierapolis-tour	\N	t	2026-04-06 11:53:04.86319+00	2026-04-06 11:53:04.86319+00	f
102	Bosphorus Cruise – Istanbul	<p>Experience one of the most iconic activities in Istanbul with a breathtaking Bosphorus cruise along the strait that divides Europe and Asia. Departing near the vibrant Spice Bazaar, this scenic journey showcases Istanbul&rsquo;s stunning skyline, featuring Ottoman palaces, mosques, and waterfront mansions. Sail past landmarks such as Dolmabah&ccedil;e Palace and historic fortresses while enjoying panoramic views of the city&rsquo;s diverse architecture. This relaxing cruise offers the perfect blend of sightseeing and leisure, making it ideal for couples, families, and first-time visitors. Whether during the day or at sunset, the Bosphorus cruise is a must-do experience that captures the essence of Turkey&rsquo;s cultural and historical beauty. Add this unforgettable journey to your Turkey holiday package with Allbound Vacations for a truly immersive experience.</p>	Bosphorus cruise Istanbul: scenic views of palaces, mosques & skyline. A must-do Turkey experience blending culture, history & relaxation.	bosphorus-cruise-istanbul	\N	t	2026-04-06 11:55:21.451629+00	2026-04-06 11:55:21.451629+00	t
99	 Spice Market Tour, Istanbul	<p>Immerse yourself in the vibrant aromas and colors of Istanbul&rsquo;s&nbsp; Spice Market on this guided tour. Located in the historic Emin&ouml;n&uuml; district, the market is a treasure trove of flavors, selling herbs, spices, teas, Turkish delight, nuts, and local delicacies. Wander through narrow alleys lined with centuries-old stalls, each offering a sensory journey that reflects Istanbul&rsquo;s rich trading heritage. Your guide will share insights into traditional Turkish culinary practices, explaining the uses of exotic spices and blends. Sample authentic delights, learn the secrets behind Turkish tea ceremonies, and pick up souvenirs that capture the essence of the city. The Spice Market experience is ideal for food lovers, culture enthusiasts, and travelers seeking an authentic taste of Istanbul. Combine history, culture, and gastronomy in a single walking tour, and make your&nbsp; Turkish holiday unforgettable with the sights, sounds, and flavors of this iconic market.</p>	Explore Istanbul’s Spice Market with its colorful stalls, aromatic spices, Turkish delights, and local flavors for an authentic Turkish experience.	spice-market-tour-istanbul	\N	t	2026-04-06 11:51:53.961493+00	2026-04-06 11:51:53.961493+00	t
