28	Tanzania	<p>Tanzania, one of Africa&rsquo;s most iconic safari destinations, offers an extraordinary blend of vast wilderness, abundant wildlife, and breathtaking landscapes. From the endless plains of the Serengeti to the wildlife-rich Ngorongoro Crater, Tanzania delivers some of the most spectacular safari experiences on the continent. It is home to the world-famous Great Migration, where millions of wildebeest and zebras move across the savannah in one of nature&rsquo;s greatest spectacles. Adventure seekers can climb Mount Kilimanjaro, Africa&rsquo;s highest peak, while beach lovers unwind on the pristine white sands of Zanzibar Island along the Indian Ocean. Tanzania&rsquo;s national parks are teeming with the Big Five, diverse birdlife, and untouched ecosystems that provide authentic, uncrowded safari experiences. With its rich culture, stunning scenery, and world-class wildlife viewing, Tanzania offers the perfect combination of adventure, relaxation, and unforgettable African travel experiences.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>	Tanzania offers iconic safaris, the Great Migration, Big Five wildlife, Mount Kilimanjaro adventures, and Zanzibar’s pristine beaches in one destination.	tanzania	1	b540da00-63c3-48c5-8dcd-9fea92650001	t	2026-02-12 19:44:13.650198+00	2026-03-24 20:02:45.714102+00	[]	\N
8	Seychelles 	<p>Escape to Seychelles, a tropical paradise of 115 breathtaking islands in the Indian Ocean. Renowned for its pristine beaches, turquoise waters, and lush greenery, Seychelles is the perfect destination for honeymooners, couples, and families seeking luxury, romance, and relaxation.</p>\n<p>With Allbound Vacations, explore the best of Seychelles through our exclusive holiday packages from Uganda, including return flights, handpicked hotels, airport transfers, and guided island experiences. Discover Mah&eacute; Island with its white-sand beaches and vibrant markets, Praslin&rsquo;s Vall&eacute;e de Mai Nature Reserve home of the rare coco de mer palm and La Digue&rsquo;s picture-perfect Anse Source d&rsquo;Argent beach.</p>\n<p>Indulge in snorkeling, diving, island-hopping cruises, hiking, or unwind with a candlelit dinner by the ocean. Seychelles blends African, French, and Asian influences, offering unique Creole cuisine and warm island hospitality.</p>\n<p>Book your Seychelles holiday from Uganda today with Allbound Vacations and experience pure island bliss. Whether it&rsquo;s a romantic honeymoon, family escape, or luxury beach getaway, Seychelles promises memories that last a lifetime.</p>	115 islands of pristine beaches, turquoise waters, and lush beauty. Perfect for honeymoons, family escapes, and luxury getaways. Explore, relax, and create unforgettable memories in pure island bliss.	seychelles	4	f65fedfc-b16c-4168-550c-de84772ca201	t	2025-10-16 21:55:07.708817+00	2026-04-11 14:46:28.17812+00	[{"question": " Where is Seychelles located?", "answer": "<p>Seychelles is an archipelago of 115 islands in the Indian Ocean, located northeast of Madagascar. It is famous for its pristine beaches, crystal-clear waters, and granite rock formations.</p>"}, {"question": " What is the best time to visit Seychelles?", "answer": "<p>Seychelles is a year-round destination, but the best months are April, May, September, and October when the seas are calm, weather is pleasant, and conditions are perfect for beach and water activities.</p>"}, {"question": "Do I need a visa to travel to Seychelles?", "answer": "<p>No visa is required for most nationalities. Travelers receive a visitor&rsquo;s permit on arrival, provided they have a valid passport, return ticket, and accommodation confirmation.</p>"}, {"question": " How many days are enough for a Seychelles holiday?", "answer": "<p>A stay of 5 to 7 nights is ideal to fully experience the islands, relax on the beaches, and enjoy excursions like island hopping and marine activities.</p>"}, {"question": "Which islands should I visit: Mah\\u00e9, Praslin, or La Digue?", "answer": "<ul>\\n<li>Mah&eacute;: Main island with international airport, culture, and nightlife</li>\\n<li>Praslin: Home to stunning beaches and nature reserves</li>\\n<li>La Digue: Peaceful, scenic, and perfect for cycling<br><br>A combination of 2&ndash;3 islands gives the best experience.</li>\\n</ul>"}, {"question": "Is Seychelles expensive, and how much should I budget?", "answer": "<p>Yes, Seychelles is considered a premium destination, but options range from budget guesthouses to luxury resorts.&nbsp;</p>"}, {"question": "What are the best beaches in Seychelles?", "answer": "<p>Some of the most famous beaches include:</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Anse Lazio (Praslin)</li>\\n<li>Anse Source d&rsquo;Argent (La Digue)</li>\\n<li>Beau Vallon (Mah&eacute;)<br><br>These are known for their clear waters, white sand, and iconic granite rocks.</li>\\n</ul>"}, {"question": "Is Seychelles safe for tourists?", "answer": "<p>Yes, Seychelles is one of the safest destinations in Africa, with low crime rates. Basic precautions like safeguarding valuables are advised.</p>"}, {"question": "What activities can I do in Seychelles besides the beach?", "answer": "<ul>\\n<li>Snorkeling &amp; scuba diving</li>\\n<li>Island hopping</li>\\n<li>Hiking &amp; nature trails</li>\\n<li>Fishing trips</li>\\n<li>Cultural tours</li>\\n<li>Sunset cruises<br><br></li>\\n</ul>"}, {"question": " Is Seychelles good for honeymooners or families?", "answer": "<p>Seychelles is perfect for both:</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Honeymooners: Romantic beaches, private villas, luxury resorts</li>\\n<li>Families: Safe environment, nature, and kid-friendly activities</li>\\n</ul>"}]	f
