2	3	[{"month": "January", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "\\u2022 Weather: Cool and pleasant, average temperature 14\\u00b0C-24\\u00b0C (57\\u00b0F-75\\u00b0F)\\n\\n\\u2022 Why Visit: Ideal for outdoor activities like desert safaris, sightseeing, and beach relaxation.\\n\\n\\u2022 Events: Dubai Shopping Festival (continues from December), offering massive discounts, entertainment, and fireworks."}, {"month": "February", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "\\u2022 Weather: Mild and comfortable, average temperature 16\\u00b0C-26\\u00b0C (61\\u00b0F-79\\u00b0F)\\n\\n\\u2022 Why Visit: Great for exploring iconic landmarks like the Burj Khalifa, Dubai Marina, and Palm Jumeirah.\\n\\n\\u2022 Events: Dubai Jazz Festival, Gulf Food Exhibition."}, {"month": "March", "rating": "good", "notes": "\\u2022 Weather: Warmer but still pleasant, average temperature 18\\u00b0C-29\\u00b0C (64\\u00b0F-84\\u00b0F)\\n\\n\\u2022 Why Visit: Outdoor activities and beach time are perfect, and the Dubai Miracle Garden is in full bloom.\\n\\n\\u2022 Events: Dubai International Boat Show, Art Dubai, Dubai World Cup (horse racing)."}, {"month": "April", "rating": "good", "notes": "\\u2022 Weather: Warming up, average temperature 21\\u00b0C-33\\u00b0C (70\\u00b0F-91\\u00b0F)\\n\\n\\u2022 Why Visit: End of the peak season, good for beach holidays and desert tours.\\n\\n\\u2022 Events: Ramadan (dates vary); during this time, public events are toned down, but it's a unique cultural experience."}, {"month": "May", "rating": "fair", "notes": "\\u2022 Weather: Hotter, average temperature 25\\u00b0C-38\\u00b0C (77\\u00b0F-100\\u00b0F)\\n\\n\\u2022 Why Visit: Fewer tourists and lower prices at hotels. Malls and indoor attractions are a good way to beat the heat.\\n\\n\\u2022 Events: Ramadan/Eid Al-Fitr (depending on the lunar calendar), Dubai Sports World begins."}, {"month": "June", "rating": "fair", "notes": "\\u2022 Weather: Very hot, average temperature 28\\u00b0C-40\\u00b0C (82\\u00b0F-104\\u00b0F)\\n\\n\\u2022 Why Visit: This is off-season; enjoy significant discounts on hotels and shopping.\\n\\n\\u2022 Events: Eid Al-Fitr, indoor activities like Ski Dubai and the Dubai Aquarium are popular."}, {"month": "July", "rating": "poor", "notes": "\\u2022 Weather: Extremely hot, average temperature 31\\u00b0C-41\\u00b0C (88\\u00b0F-106\\u00b0F)\\n\\n\\u2022 Why Visit: Stay cool indoors with world-class shopping malls, theme parks, and indoor activities.\\n\\n\\u2022 Events: Dubai Summer Surprises (shopping deals, entertainment)."}, {"month": "August", "rating": "poor", "notes": "\\u2022 Weather: Extremely hot, average temperature 32\\u00b0C-42\\u00b0C (90\\u00b0F-108\\u00b0F)\\n\\n\\u2022 Why Visit: Similar to July, indoor activities dominate. Excellent discounts on accommodation and attractions.\\n\\n\\u2022 Events: Dubai Summer Surprises continues, Eid Al-Adha celebrations."}, {"month": "September", "rating": "fair", "notes": "\\u2022 Weather: Hot, but slightly cooler towards the end, average temperature 29\\u00b0C-39\\u00b0C (84\\u00b0F-102\\u00b0F)\\n\\n\\u2022 Why Visit: As temperatures begin to drop, outdoor activities like evening desert safaris become more enjoyable.\\n\\n\\u2022 Events: Dubai Home Festival, Dubai International Dance Festival."}, {"month": "October", "rating": "good", "notes": "\\u2022 Weather: Warm and comfortable, average temperature 25\\u00b0C-36\\u00b0C (77\\u00b0F-97\\u00b0F)\\n\\n\\u2022 Why Visit: Outdoor season returns; ideal for beach days, water sports, and sightseeing.\\n\\n\\u2022 Events: Dubai Opera season, Halloween-themed events."}, {"month": "November", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "\\u2022 Weather: Pleasant, average temperature 20\\u00b0C-31\\u00b0C (68\\u00b0F-88\\u00b0F)\\n\\n\\u2022 Why Visit: Perfect time for exploring Dubai's outdoor attractions like Al Fahidi Historical Neighborhood, Dubai Frame, and beach resorts.\\n\\n\\u2022 Events: Dubai Design Week, DP World Tour Championship (golf), Downtown Design."}, {"month": "December", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "\\u2022 Weather: Cool and breezy, average temperature 16\\u00b0C-26\\u00b0C (61\\u00b0F-79\\u00b0F)\\n\\n\\u2022 Why Visit: Dubai\\u2019s peak season for tourism; enjoy holiday lights, New Year\\u2019s Eve fireworks, and winter festivals.\\n\\n\\u2022 Events: Dubai Shopping Festival kicks off, National Day Celebrations (December 2), Christmas and New Year's Eve festivities."}]	<p>The best time to visit Dubai is from November to March, when the weather is pleasantly warm, the skies are clear, and the city bursts with outdoor experiences. This peak travel season is perfect for beach days, evening desert safaris, rooftop dining, and exploring Dubai&rsquo;s most iconic attractions like the Burj Khalifa and Dubai Marina. Travelers enjoy comfortable temperatures and world-class events such as the Dubai Shopping Festival. From April to October, Dubai becomes extremely hot, creating a low-season ideal for budget-friendly travel, indoor adventures, luxury shopping, and thrilling theme parks. Whatever the season, Dubai promises excitement, luxury, and unforgettable memories.</p>	2025-11-05 21:17:51.920523+00	2025-11-15 19:54:28.099379+00
3	7	[{"month": "January", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "Hot, tropical, and vibrant, perfect for beach holidays, resort stays, and enjoying the island\\u2019s lively summer atmosphere despite occasional rain."}, {"month": "February", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "Warm ocean waters and great beach conditions make it ideal for relaxation and luxury travel, though humidity and brief showers can occur."}, {"month": "March", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "Weather improves with less rain, making it excellent for snorkeling, diving, and full-day island excursions."}, {"month": "April", "rating": "good", "notes": "Pleasant temperatures and reduced humidity create a great balance for both beach time and sightseeing activities."}, {"month": "May", "rating": "good", "notes": "Start of the dry season with cooler weather\\u2014ideal for hiking, nature tours, and comfortable exploration."}, {"month": "June", "rating": "good", "notes": "Cooler and less humid, making it perfect for budget travel, sightseeing, and outdoor adventures."}, {"month": "July", "rating": "fair", "notes": "The coolest and windiest month, better suited for surfing and kitesurfing than swimming or sunbathing."}, {"month": "August", "rating": "good", "notes": "Conditions improve with more sunshine, making it suitable for a mix of beach activities and excursions."}, {"month": "September", "rating": "good", "notes": "Warmer temperatures and calmer winds offer excellent conditions for all-round travel and outdoor experiences."}, {"month": "October", "rating": "fair", "notes": "A transitional month with rising temperatures\\u2014still enjoyable but slightly less consistent compared to peak months.\\n"}, {"month": "November", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "One of the best months, warm, dry, and perfect for beaches, diving, and luxury holidays.\\n"}, {"month": "December", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "Hot, festive, and lively, ideal for holiday travel, beach relaxation, and end-of-year getaways."}]	<p>The best time to visit Mauritius is between May and December, when the island enjoys warm, sunny weather with temperatures ranging from the high 20s to around 30&deg;C. These months offer ideal conditions for beach holidays, swimming, and outdoor adventures. That said, Mauritius is a year-round destination, with each season offering something unique. The summer months are great for surfing and water sports, while June to October is the perfect period for whale watching. In October, the island comes alive with colorful celebrations like Diwali, the Festival of Lights. The peak travel season runs from December to March, when travelers flock to the island to escape the winter chill &mdash; expect higher prices and more visitors during this period.</p>	2025-11-11 19:14:45.588591+00	2026-04-05 18:16:44.168501+00
1	8	[{"month": "January", "rating": "fair", "notes": "Hot, humid, and wetter due to northwest monsoon winds. Still good for beach relaxation and resorts, but not ideal for diving or outdoor-heavy itineraries."}, {"month": "February", "rating": "fair", "notes": "Similar to January with occasional heavy showers. Best suited for honeymooners seeking quiet luxury rather than activity-focused trips."}, {"month": "March", "rating": "good", "notes": "Weather improves with calmer seas and less rain. A great transition month for snorkeling, island hopping, and light outdoor activities."}, {"month": "April", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "One of the best months to visit Seychelles. Calm seas, minimal wind, and outstanding visibility for diving and marine activities."}, {"month": "May", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "Comfortable temperatures, low humidity, and lush landscapes. Perfect for both beach holidays and inland exploration like hiking."}, {"month": "June", "rating": "good", "notes": "Start of southeast trade winds. Cooler and breezy, ideal for surfing and sailing, though some beaches may be rough."}, {"month": "July", "rating": "good", "notes": "Windy but dry and cooler. Best for active travelers, hiking, and nature experiences rather than pure beach relaxation."}, {"month": "August", "rating": "fair", "notes": "Continues with breezy conditions. Great for adventure, water sports, and exploring multiple islands.\\n"}, {"month": "September", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "Winds begin to ease, seas calm down, and conditions improve significantly for swimming, snorkeling, and beach holidays."}, {"month": "October", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "Perfect weather balance ; calm waters, warm temperatures, and top-tier diving visibility. Ideal for luxury and romantic travel."}, {"month": "November", "rating": "good", "notes": "Transition back to warmer conditions with occasional showers. Still great for beach holidays and fewer crowds."}, {"month": "December", "rating": "fair", "notes": "Hot, humid, and wetter again, but popular due to festive travel. Good for holiday vibes, though weather can be unpredictable."}]	<p>The best time to visit Seychelles is during the calmer trade-wind transition months: April to May and October to November. These periods offer clear waters, gentle winds, and perfect beach weather, making them ideal for swimming, snorkeling, diving, and island-hopping.</p>\n<p>Seychelles experiences two main trade winds each year:</p>\n<p>Northwest trade winds &ndash; November to March</p>\n<p>Southeast trade winds &ndash; May to September</p>\n<p>During the southeast monsoon, some beaches may have seaweed accumulation, so it&rsquo;s wise to choose your island or resort location carefully depending on the time of year.</p>\n<p>Temperatures in Seychelles stay warm year-round, averaging around 30&deg;C (86&deg;F) with a mix of sunshine and short tropical showers. Due to its location just seven degrees south of the Equator and being surrounded by the vast Indian Ocean, the weather can be unpredictable, and online forecasts are not always reliable.</p>\n<p>Whether you visit in the dry season or monsoon months, Seychelles promises breathtaking beaches, turquoise waters, and unforgettable island experiences all year long.</p>	2025-11-05 15:02:25.174512+00	2026-04-11 14:32:25.395683+00
