4	2	[{"month": "January", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "January is hot and mostly dry, with clear skies and excellent visibility. It\\u2019s a prime time for gorilla and chimpanzee trekking, as forest trails are dry and wildlife movements are easier to follow."}, {"month": "February", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "February remains dry and sunny, making it ideal for gorilla trekking in the south and classic safaris. Northern Uganda can be hot and dusty, but overall conditions are excellent for travel."}, {"month": "March", "rating": "good", "notes": "March signals the start of the first rains. Landscapes begin to freshen up, wildlife gives birth, and birdwatching improves, making it a rewarding month for nature lovers."}, {"month": "April", "rating": "poor", "notes": "April is the wettest month of the year. Travel can be challenging due to muddy roads, but this is the best time for discounted lodge rates and permits and quiet parks."}, {"month": "May", "rating": "poor", "notes": "Rainfall reduces slightly in May. The countryside is green and scenic, offering peaceful travel with fewer visitors and improving road conditions."}, {"month": "June", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "June marks the beginning of the peak safari season. Weather conditions are excellent for gorilla trekking and wildlife viewing, and advance bookings are strongly recommended."}, {"month": "July", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "July offers some of the best safari and trekking conditions. Trails are dry, wildlife gathers near water sources, and visibility in national parks is outstanding."}, {"month": "August", "rating": "good", "notes": "August is another top safari month, ideal for big game viewing, including elephants, lions, and sometimes leopards, across Uganda\\u2019s national parks."}, {"month": "September", "rating": "fair", "notes": "September sits between dry and wet seasons. Occasional rains may occur, but travelers benefit from lower costs and quieter parks"}, {"month": "October", "rating": "fair", "notes": "October is calm and less crowded. While rain can be unpredictable, gorilla permits and accommodation deals are often available."}, {"month": "November", "rating": "good", "notes": "November is wetter, turning Uganda lush and green. Fewer tourists visit, making it suitable for travelers seeking solitude and scenic landscapes."}, {"month": "December", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "December marks the return of drier conditions. It\\u2019s a great month for safaris, birdwatching, and holiday travel, with migratory birds arriving across the country."}]	<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Ebrima;">The climate is good in Uganda all year round, day time temperatures generally hovering between 24 -28C. It cools down considerably at night, enough for a jersey but woolens are not necessary. The rains come twice a year, in October/November (short rains) and mid- March to end of May. Rainy season is no reason to postpone travel however, as generally it rains for an hour and the rest of the day is clear and sunny.</span></p>	2025-12-13 20:46:20.180444+00	2026-03-26 21:24:23.999832+00
6	26	[{"month": "January", "rating": "fair", "notes": "Cold winter conditions dominate, especially in cities like Istanbul. Ideal for snow experiences and cultural sightseeing, but not suitable for beach holidays. "}, {"month": "February", "rating": "fair", "notes": "Still wintery and cold, with occasional snow. Best for indoor attractions, shopping, and fewer crowds at historical sites."}, {"month": "March", "rating": "good", "notes": "Weather begins to warm up, making it a good time for city tours and exploring landmarks like Hagia Sophia with fewer tourists.\\n"}, {"month": "April", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "Spring blooms across Turkey, especially during the famous Istanbul Tulip Festival. Perfect weather for sightseeing and photography."}, {"month": "May", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "One of the best months to visit\\u2014warm, sunny, and ideal for both cultural tours and early beach experiences along the coast."}, {"month": "June", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "Start of summer with great beach weather in places like Antalya, combined with excellent conditions for excursions.\\n"}, {"month": "July", "rating": "good", "notes": "Hot and sunny, perfect for beach holidays, though inland cities can be very warm. Ideal for coastal destinations."}, {"month": "August", "rating": "good", "notes": "Peak summer heat continues. Best for beach lovers and resort stays, especially along the Mediterranean coast."}, {"month": "September", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "Temperatures become more comfortable, making it one of the best months for both sightseeing and beach holidays."}, {"month": "October", "rating": "excellent", "notes": "Mild weather and fewer crowds, perfect for exploring cities, historical sites, and coastal regions."}, {"month": "November", "rating": "good", "notes": "Cooler temperatures set in, suitable for cultural trips and city exploration without the summer crowds.\\n"}, {"month": "December", "rating": "good", "notes": "Cold and wintery again, especially in inland areas. Best for festive city breaks and cultural experiences rather than outdoor travel."}]	<p>Turkey offers a rich and diverse travel experience year-round, thanks to its unique position between Europe and Asia and its varied climate. The country experiences four distinct seasons, each offering something special for travelers. Spring (April to May) and autumn (September to October) are widely considered the best times to visit, with mild temperatures, blooming landscapes, and ideal conditions for sightseeing across cities like Istanbul and natural wonders such as Cappadocia. Summer (June to August) is perfect for beach holidays along the Mediterranean coast, especially in destinations like Antalya, though temperatures can be quite high inland. Winter (December to February) brings colder weather and snow, creating a magical setting for cultural tours and unique experiences. Overall, Turkey is a year-round destination with seasonal highlights suited to every type of traveler.</p>	2026-04-06 07:06:43.074354+00	2026-04-06 07:06:43.074354+00
