56	package	37	5	\N	Chimpanzee Tracking in Kibale, Drive to Queen Elizabeth National Park (approximately 185km/3hrs),	Start your day with an unforgettable adventure! After breakfast, head to the park offices for a 7:30 am briefing, then venture into the forest to track the fascinating chimpanzees. Upon sighting spend 1 hour observing these incredible creatures up close, watching them go about their daily routine - from playful antics and grooming sessions to feeding and caring for their young. Witness their agility as they swing through the trees, and experience the thrill of being in the presence of our closest animal relatives. This unique encounter is sure to leave you with lifelong memories!\n\nReturn to the lodge a for a warm lunch and refreshing shower, check out and drive to Queen Elizabeth National Park through the stunning crater lakes region and the charming old town of Fort Portal, nestled in the foothills of the majestic Rwenzori Mountains.\n\n As you approach Queen Elizabeth Park, take in the breathtaking views of the mountain ranges. Before checking into your lodge, consider visiting the salt pans of Katwe and a volcanic crater lake. \nArrive at your lodge in time for lunch and relaxation, followed by an evening game drive in the mating grounds of the Uganda Kobs. Search for lions, elephants, buffaloes, and other wild animals in their natural habitat, immersing yourself in the beauty of African wildlife.	Queen Elizabeth National Park, Kasese, Western Region, Uganda	0.18285620	30.22780220	Overnight at Kyambura Gorge Lodge.  Buffalo Lodge for midrange \nMeal Plan: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner	2026-03-14 21:11:45.664517+00	\N
